; FILED: a nested vector BUILT AT RUNTIME is rejected natively while the
; identical LITERAL is accepted — NATIVE is the wrong side.
; (vector (vector 1.0 2.0) (vector 3.0 4.0)) and #(#(1.0 2.0) #(3.0 4.0)) are
; the same value, so they must coerce to the same 2x2 tensor.
; native -r : "caught" (raises) for the built form, (2 2) for the literal
; vm        : (2 2) for both
; The VM's coercion is value-based and therefore consistent; native's depends on
; how the value was produced. Native codegen is not VM-owned, so this is filed
; rather than "fixed" in the VM to match. Gate it in
; corpus/41_tensor_literals.esk once native accepts the built form.
(display (guard (e (#t "caught")) (tensor-shape (vector (vector 1.0 2.0) (vector 3.0 4.0)))))
(newline)
(display (guard (e (#t "caught")) (tensor-shape #(#(1.0 2.0) #(3.0 4.0)))))
(newline)
